Z||000000||Seanh||12-30-2000||05:13 PM||||I was messin around on my new computer and I downloaded it little application that helps you fill out online forms by inserting all your previously saved information in the correct form blanks. Now, this morning I check my email and had 11 messages. 2 of them were from real people, the rest were spam. Saying I needed to reply back to confirm my subscription to all these usless emailings. That only thing I can think of that did this might be Gator, only thing I downloaded or signed up for. I just report all the spam to <A HREF="http://www.spamcop.net" TARGET=_blank>www.spamcop.net</A>  and usally dont get any more crap from that person. Anyone know if Gator sells your email address to mass mailing lists?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
